# Feature Test Coverage (mandatory — never skip)

**A feature is NOT shippable without full automated test coverage.** Every scenario the feature supports must have a corresponding test. No exceptions.

## Required surfaces (mirror AI prompt rule)

When a feature is user-visible on a surface, that surface needs tests:

| Surface | Integration spec location |
|---------|----------------------------|
| Dashboard | `backend/src/modules/ai/*.integration.spec.ts` |
| Service provider mobile | `backend/src/modules/provider-mobile/provider-ai-*.integration.spec.ts` |
| Customer mobile | `backend/src/modules/ai/customer-ai-command.integration.spec.ts` |
| Public booking web | `backend/src/modules/public-booking/*.spec.ts` + `public-booking-assistant.schema.spec.ts` |

## Definition of done

Before marking a feature complete, verify ALL of the following:

1. **Unit tests** (`*.spec.ts` next to source or `*.util.spec.ts`):
   - Every exported function / public method
   - Every branch: happy path, validation failure, missing params, edge inputs
   - Prompt detection helpers (`is*Prompt`, `extract*FromPrompt`, `decompose*`)
   - Rescue paths, heuristic enrichment, validator rules
   - Use `it.each` over fixture arrays — one test per scenario `id`

2. **Integration tests** (`*.integration.spec.ts`):
   - End-to-end handler flow with mocked deps (Nest `Test.createTestingModule`)
   - Multi-step compound execution (check → mutate → follow-up)
   - Session/context propagation between steps
   - Error paths with clear user-facing summaries (no slot, missing service, etc.)
   - Schema/classifier wiring tests where prompts are classified

3. **100% scenario coverage** — every entry in `*.fixtures.ts` must be exercised:
   - Fixtures drive `it.each` in both unit and integration specs
   - If a scenario exists in fixtures, a test must assert it — no orphan prompts
   - Add new scenarios to fixtures FIRST, then add matching tests

4. **Coverage thresholds** — new modules must meet project gates:
   - AI modules: aim for 100% statements/functions/lines (see `test:ai-providers`, `test:sprint14`)
   - Run the relevant `npm run test:*` script and fix failures before shipping
   - Add a `test:*` script in `package.json` when a feature domain is new

## Required file pattern per feature

```
feature-name.fixtures.ts          # scenarios + classifier rules
feature-name.util.ts              # logic + decomposition
feature-name.util.spec.ts         # unit: detection, decomposition, rescue
feature-name.integration.spec.ts  # integration: handlers, compounds, validation
```

## Agent workflow (blocking)

When implementing or reviewing ANY feature:

- [ ] Create fixtures with all NL scenarios (tag `surface` per prompt) before writing handlers
- [ ] Unit tests: `it.each` over every fixture `id`
- [ ] Integration tests: end-to-end per applicable surface (dashboard, provider mobile, customer mobile, public booking)
- [ ] Run tests locally; zero failures
- [ ] **Do not mark TODO `[x]`, merge, or say "done" without unit + integration specs**

Reference implementation: `ai-cmd-h1` — 82 unit + integration tests, 30 prompt variants, `test:ai-providers` gate.

